perate and I can see  how a lot of people have a problem with  that we know that i think twenty five  percent of revenues  casinos come from addicted gamblers so  it is a big problem according to this  book it's more than twenty-five percent  and that's a really interesting thing  you often hear the casino industry say  hey listen problem gambling is not  really an issue only one to two percent  of the population are problem gamblers  but what that doesn't consider is that a  lot of the population doesn't go to  casinos so a more relevant question is  well what percentage of people that  regularly go to casinos or problem  gamblers the number goes way up and as  Pat is suggesting a significantly a  disproportionately high percentage of  profits Pat cited 25% it may be that it  may be as high as 35 or 40 percent of  casino profits that come from problem  gamblers and the book covers all of this  and more so I really encourage you to  check it out we are talking about the  book addiction by design by Natasha  Dowie Shaw hopefully she'll be joining  us on the show for an interview sooner  than later and you can check out all of  my recommendations at david pakman.com  slash recommendations i'm on twitter at  d pakman the show is on twitter at david  pakman show we really have an  extraordinary program coming up for you  today
 

